message: "If you use this software or its method, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Structure-preserving physics-informed learning of open quantum dynamics with spectral-frame encodings and operator-system truncation"
authors:
  - family-names: Huynh
    given-names: Molena
    email: molena.huynh@jmp.com
    affiliation: "North Carolina State University, Raleigh, North Carolina 27695, USA"
abstract: >-
  A structure-preserving, physics-informed framework for identifying Markovian
  open quantum systems. A Cholesky density network makes unphysical states
  unrepresentable; a spectral-frame (interaction-picture) parameterization learns
  only the slow envelope in the Hamiltonian eigenbasis and supplies the fast Bohr
  oscillations analytically; and an operator-system spectral truncation
  band-limits the generator to its slow Bohr modes, yielding a controlled
  hierarchy from the secular (Davies) generator through the rotating-wave
  approximation to the exact generator with an a posteriori error certificate.
  Part of the spectral-truncation operators (specops) program.
